# ⚡ Performance

## Core Web Vitals Targets
- LCP < 2.5s, FID < 100ms, CLS < 0.1, TTFB < 600ms

## Bundle Size Budgets
- Initial JS < 200KB gzipped
- Initial CSS < 50KB gzipped
- Page weight < 1MB initial
- Third-party < 50KB combined

## Images
- Use Next.js `<Image>` component
- Modern formats (WebP, AVIF) with fallbacks
- Lazy load below fold
- Width/height to prevent CLS
- Placeholder blur for better UX

## Code Splitting
- Dynamic imports for heavy components/modals
- Lazy load non-critical features
- Prefetch critical routes

## Server Components (Next.js)
- Default to Server Components
- Client only for: useState, useEffect, events, browser APIs
- Keep Client Components small and leaf-level
- Fetch data in Server Components

## Data Fetching
- Parallel fetching (avoid waterfalls): `Promise.all()`
- Cache with proper revalidation
- Use `loading.tsx` for streaming
- Paginate large lists
- Debounce search inputs

## React Optimization
- `useMemo` for expensive calculations
- `useCallback` for callbacks passed to children
- `React.memo()` for expensive components
- Virtualize long lists
- Avoid inline object/array creation
- Stable, unique keys for lists

## Fonts & Scripts
- Use `next/font` for optimization
- Preload critical fonts
- `font-display: swap`
- Async third-party scripts
- Use Next.js `<Script strategy="afterInteractive">`

## CSS
- Tailwind JIT mode
- Avoid CSS-in-JS for critical path
- Remove unused CSS

## Database & API
- Index queries properly
- Cache results
- Connection pooling
- Paginate large sets
- SELECT specific fields
- Avoid N+1 queries

## Monitoring
- Track Core Web Vitals in production
- Performance budgets in CI/CD
- Lighthouse CI automated checks

## Checklist
- [ ] Lighthouse score > 90
- [ ] Core Web Vitals met
- [ ] Images optimized, lazy loaded
- [ ] Bundle size within budget
- [ ] Server Components used where possible
- [ ] Fonts optimized with next/font
- [ ] Database queries indexed
